title: The forest as a query provider
tags: [[Query engine]]
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: The forest resolves path operands to nodes, and rewrites the two leaves no bitmap holds — :path and an order-sensitive osm path — into uuid_in sets.

Before evaluation, `routes::prepare_indexed_query` asks the forest
([[The tree cache]]) for what only it can answer:

|!Step |!Applies to |!Hands the evaluator |
|path targets |`->`, `->*`, `=>*` with a path |the node, in `QueryRoots.path` |
|exact nodes |`=`/`!=` with a string on a `tree_ref`, `:parent = "<path>"` |the node or `None` — "resolved, no such node" — in `QueryRoots.node` |
|forest leaves (`forest_query::resolve_path_leaves`) |the `:path` aspect; an `osm` path with several terms or a `/` |the `uuid_in` set it matches, in place of the leaf |
|sort keys |a `tree_ref` sort |`SortKeys`, the path keys rebuilt from the forest |

The `Option` of an exact node is load-bearing: a `None` entry means "resolved, and it is
no node" (an empty result), a ''missing'' entry "nobody resolved it" — a daemon bug, so
the operand can never be answered from the wrong (name-based) bitmap.

Rewriting a forest leaf does not walk the whole forest when it can help it:

* a `:path` comparison ''seeks'' (`PathSeek`): an exact path goes down its names, one read per level; a pattern anchored on a literal prefix seeks the prefix's folder; an ordering enters only the subtrees that can fall on the right side. `:path` ''presence'' needs no walk at all — a node has a path exactly when it has a position;
* an `osm` path starts from the ''anchors'' of its last term, verifies each anchor's path, and takes its subtree, which the evaluator expands from its descendant bitmap; the anchors are first cut to the folders of an earlier, rarer term when that is cheaper;
* what is left — an unanchored regex over paths, a last term ending with the separator — walks the stored forest.

The rewrite must be deterministic: the cursor is bound to a hash of the rewritten
query ([[How queries are evaluated]]). A field with no forest is the benign case: the
leaf matches nothing, and the rewrite says so. `tests/path_aspect.rs` and
`tests/index_oracle.rs` hold it to the oracle; `tests/kv_cost.rs` to its bounds.
